     <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n\n                \n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Data Analytics Made Accessible by Dr. Anil Mahehswari<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Data Science for Business: What You Need to Know about Data Mining and Data-Analytic Thinking by Foster Provost and Tom Fawcett<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Business unIntelligence: Insight and Innovation beyond Analytics and Big Data by Dr. Barry Devlin<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Storytelling with Data: A Data Visualization Guide for Business Professionals by Cole Nussbaumer Knaflic<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Big Data: A Revolution That Will Transform How We Live, Work, and Think by Kenneth Cukier and Viktor Mayer-Sch\u00f6nberger<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Artificial Intelligence- A Guide for Thinking Humans By Melanie Mitchell<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Hundred-Page Machine Learning Book by Andriy Burkov<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Naked Statistics: Stripping the Dread from the Data by Charles Wheelan<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Python for Data Analysis: Data Wrangling with Pandas, NumPy, and Jupyter by Wes McKinney<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Learning R: A Step-By-Step Function Guide to Data Analysis by Richard Cotton<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Data Analytics Made Accessible<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p> &#8211; <strong><em>Dr. Anil Mahehswari<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"183\" height=\"276\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/data-analytics-made-accessible.webp\" alt=\" Data Analytics Made Accessible - Data Analytics Book\" class=\"wp-image-12762\" style=\"width:188px;height:auto\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are taking your initial steps as a data analyst, this is the most comprehensive book for you to learn and master everything from the beginning. The language is easy, and the chapters are organized like an introductory college course. It contains an array of real-world examples to enhance your understanding. Hence, many universities are adopting it in their syllabus.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It discusses data analytics tools, applications, and other basic and advanced concepts. The best part is it perfectly combines theory and practical examples, so you can understand the \u2018what\u2019 and \u2018how\u2019 of data analytics.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Although it was originally published in 2014, it has gone through several updates over the years to include all the essential topics, such as artificial intelligence, big data, data privacy, and data science career guidance.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Business Intelligence Concepts &amp; Applications<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Instances of data analysis in action in the real world<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Data analytics lifecycle, starting from data collection to visualization<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Decision trees, regression models, and cluster analysis<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Data warehousing and Data mining<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Data modeling primer<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Case studies to show the impact of data analysis across different industries&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Review inquiries to help you check your knowledge&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211;<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Data-Analytics-Made-Accessible-2018-ebook\/dp\/B00K2I2JL8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analytics Made Accessible<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Data Science for Business: What You Need to Know about Data Mining and Data-Analytic Thinking<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Foster Provost and Tom Fawcett<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"570\" height=\"750\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/data-science-for-business.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12763\" style=\"width:215px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/data-science-for-business.webp 570w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/data-science-for-business-228x300.webp 228w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 570px) 100vw, 570px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>If you want to understand the mechanics of data-driven decision-making, this is an ideal data analytics book to start with. It will help you lay a strong foundation by delving into the importance of data for business decisions.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>As a data analyst beginner, this book introduces you to how data science and business work together and how to make data-driven decisions. It helps you connect the dots between data and business applications. You get an insight into the process that companies use to make informed decisions like customer churn rate and expected sales.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The authors have done an excellent job of explaining key data science concepts in easy-to-understand language for non-technical readers without compromising on details. They have outlined principles and techniques of data science without getting too much into the technical details of algorithms.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This book will teach you to think analytically and use data as a secret weapon to sustain in today\u2019s competitive world.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Techniques like decision trees, regression analysis, and clustering<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Business problems and data science solution<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>How data science fits into business decision-making<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Predictive modeling: from correlation to supervised segmentation<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Visualizing model performance<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Decision analytic thinking<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Real-world case studies involving data analytics to make a measurable impact<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211; <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Data-science-Business-Foster-Provost\/dp\/935110267X\/ref=tmm_pap_swatch_0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Science for Business: What You Need to Know about Data Mining and Data-Analytic Thinking<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. <strong>Business UnIntelligence: Insight and Innovation beyond Analytics and Big Data&nbsp;<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Dr. Barry Devlin<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"335\" height=\"500\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/business-unIntelligence.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12764\" style=\"width:198px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/business-unIntelligence.webp 335w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/business-unIntelligence-201x300.webp 201w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 335px) 100vw, 335px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>For readers who want an overview of business intelligence, it\u2019s the perfect find. It explores how the trinity of people, information, and processes come together to ensure business success in this modern world.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It discusses various conventional methods of BI, their weaknesses and strengths, and suggestions for the future. Dr. Devlin is the pioneer of data warehousing and has made substantial contributions to BI.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>He has not talked about traditional business intelligence concepts but outlines how BI can fall short while sharing new models and frameworks for improved practices. The book guides you to progress in the business intelligence field, giving an overview of the past, present, and future of BI.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The genesis of the business-technology ecosystem<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Data, information, and the hegemony of IT<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Why businesses need logical, data-based, and interactive decision-making&nbsp;<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>How applications became apps and other process peculiarities<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Practical tips for using big data<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Innovation in the human and social realm<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211; <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Business-unIntelligence-Insight-Innovation-Analytics\/dp\/1935504568\/ref=tmm_pap_swatch_0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Business UnIntelligence: Insight and Innovation beyond Analytics and Big Data&nbsp;<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Storytelling with Data: A Data Visualization Guide for Business Professionals<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Cole Nussbaumer Knaflic<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"602\" height=\"750\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/storytelling-with-data.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12765\" style=\"width:217px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/storytelling-with-data.webp 602w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/storytelling-with-data-241x300.webp 241w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 602px) 100vw, 602px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Any data is as good as the story you choose to tell using it. Numbers on a spreadsheet are of no use if you don\u2019t know how to present them meaningfully to extract actionable insights.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It is one of the best data analytics books for beginners, taking you through the fundamentals of communicating with data through visualization and storytelling. It focuses on a vital aspect of data analytics, i.e., communication.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The author explains how to transform data into a compelling story by combining theory with real-world examples. It also talks about how to use data analytics tools more effectively, making it a must-read for professionals who need to present data to stakeholders.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Correct visualization for the right situation<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Best practices for creating clean and impactful data visualizations<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Create presentations using multiple visuals and tell an intriguing story<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The psychology behind how people interpret data<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Thinking like a visual designer<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Eliminating clutter and focusing on the most important aspects of data<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Real-world examples of compelling data storytelling in a business context<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211; <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Storytelling-Data-Visualization-Business-Professionals\/dp\/1119002257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Storytelling with Data: A Data Visualization Guide for Business Professionals<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n        <div class=\"container position-relative mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"row pb-4\">\n                <h2 style=\"font-size:32px\">Upcoming Masterclass<\/h2>\n                <p>Attend our live classes led by experienced and desiccated instructors of Wscube Tech.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"owl-carousel myOwl\">\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cracking-meta-google-ads-2026-data-automation-attribution?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n      