038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-07T104930_382_1786105407836_186872.webp\" alt=\"Booming Digital Marketing Career in AI Era\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cybersecurity-professional-career-roadmap-2026-2?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-05T122121_005_1786351858212_930412.webp\" alt=\"Cybersecurity Professional Career Roadmap 2026\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Big Data: A Revolution That Will Transform How We Live, Work, and Think<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Kenneth Cukier and Viktor Mayer-Sch\u00f6nberger<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"337\" height=\"500\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/big-data.webp\" alt=\"Big Data - Top Data Analytics Book\" class=\"wp-image-12766\" style=\"width:205px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/big-data.webp 337w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/big-data-202x300.webp 202w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 337px) 100vw, 337px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Anyone who is involved in data analytics must have heard of big data. Here is the finest book to understand why data analytics is important beyond the corporate sense. Authored by two experts in the field, the book highlights how big data is changing our world for the better (and sometimes worse).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>As you read the book, you will get to know how data analytics is used across varied businesses and can affect any industry. It will help you to embrace the impending changes in the business and prepare you for the fact that big data is here to stay.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>You will not just find technical content related to big data algorithms but also understand what it is, what it can do, and its possible impact on the future. It contains facts related to how big data can reveal insights that can\u2019t be found otherwise.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The obsolescence of sampling<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Shift in industry and government to collect data<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The acceptance of increased measurement error in return for more data<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Move away from the age-old search for causality<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ways to control the \u201cdatafication\u201d of human life<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211; <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Big-Data-Revolution-Transform-Think\/dp\/0544002695\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Big Data: A Revolution That Will Transform How We Live, Work, and Think<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">6. Artificial Intelligence- A Guide for Thinking Humans<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Melanie Mitchell<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"307\" height=\"500\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/artificial-intelligence.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12767\" style=\"width:198px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/artificial-intelligence.webp 307w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/artificial-intelligence-184x300.webp 184w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 307px) 100vw, 307px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Written by Melanie Mitchell, a renowned computer scientist, this book explores the history of artificial intelligence, its achievements, aspirations, and growing concerns. It helps you comprehend challenging concepts like natural language processing, neural networks, and machine vision models while assessing the growth of AI and people who were involved in its development throughout history.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The book blurs the line between the hype around AI and real advances in the field. You will come across various pressing issues in the field of AI today, including its functioning. The book will help you understand if you should be concerned about AI overtaking human tasks by sharing the stories behind the science of AI.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Yes, as a data analyst, you may not need a thorough understanding of AI. Still, it is among the best books for data analysis to get a sneak peek into AI technologies and their impact on the data analytics sector.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>History of AI<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>How the different approaches to AI work, including Deep Learning and Machine Learning<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Approaches to game-playing AI<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Neural networks and deep learning<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Common sense and how it remains a significant challenge for AI systems<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Human vs. Machine Intelligence<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>AI projects, such as Cyc\u2019<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ethical and Societal Implications of AI<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211; <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Artificial-Intelligence-Thinking-Humans-Pelican-ebook\/dp\/B07QPR8W6V\/ref=tmm_kin_swatch_0\">Artificial Intelligence- A Guide for Thinking Humans<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">7. The Hundred-Page Machine Learning Book&nbsp;<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Andriy Burkov<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"349\" height=\"453\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/hundred-page-machine-learning-book.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12768\" style=\"width:226px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/hundred-page-machine-learning-book.webp 349w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/hundred-page-machine-learning-book-231x300.webp 231w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 349px) 100vw, 349px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>As evident by the name, this book provides a machine learning overview in just over 100 pages. The author has introduced the subject comprehensively, making it an easy and interesting read for learners with no prior knowledge of programming or statistics.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The book may seem short, but it covers ample information, including topics like neural networks, hyperparameter tuning, and cluster analysis. These terms may sound overwhelming and difficult to beginners, but the book explains them in easy language.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can complete the book in a few days or hours and gain a wealth of knowledge. It contains concise and clear articles on various machine learning concepts explained with mathematical-related topics used in the data analysis field.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Notation and Definitions<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Best machine learning algorithms<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Neural networks and deep learning<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Advanced and other forms of learning<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211; <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Hundred-Page-Machine-Learning-Book\/dp\/1999579518\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">The Hundred-Page Machine Learning Book<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">8 Naked Statistics: Stripping the Dread from the Data<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Charles Wheelan<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"267\" height=\"400\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/naked-statistics.webp\" alt=\"Naked Statistics - Analyitcs Book for Data Analytics\" class=\"wp-image-12769\" style=\"width:223px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/naked-statistics.webp 267w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/naked-statistics-200x300.webp 200w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 267px) 100vw, 267px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Statistics can be intimidating, but Kudos to Charles Wheelan, who explains tricky statistical concepts in an engaging and educational way. So, if you need to brush up on your college statistics or are struggling with arithmetic ideas presented as a list of numbers and symbols but without context, this is among the best books for data analysis to pick.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>For anyone who gets stressed seeing numbers and technical jargon, this book will work wonders by making data analytics easier to understand. The author explains key concepts of statistical analysis, such as regression, correlation, and inference, in an interesting way. You will see Wheelan making a point regarding how everyone, not just data experts, needs to understand statistics in this contemporary world.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The book is light on math but heavy on practical applications, so it appeals to learners more than other books. It may not transform you into a statistics master, but it will add value to your statistics education by helping you learn the underlying ideas and why they are important.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Descriptive statistics<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Interpreting data accurately and avoiding common errors<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Correlation, basic probability, inference, and regression analysis<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>How statistics is used in various aspects of the real world, such as politics, sports, and business<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Core statistical concepts without indulging in tricky mathematical numbers and terms<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211; <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Naked-Statistics-Stripping-Dread-Data\/dp\/039334777X\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Naked Statistics: Stripping the Dread from the Data<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">9. Python for Data Analysis: Data Wrangling with pandas, NumPy, and Jupyter<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Wes McKinney<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"381\" height=\"500\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/python-for-data-analysis.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12770\" style=\"width:239px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/python-for-data-analysis.webp 381w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/python-for-data-analysis-229x300.webp 229w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 381px) 100vw, 381px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>If you are familiar with <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Python<\/a> and object-oriented programming, this book is for you. It skips the theoretical part and emphasizes hands-on knowledge, guiding you to mastering Python for data analysis.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We know that Python is a go-to language for data analysts, and this book explores why. It educates you about <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/python\/libraries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Python libraries<\/a>, such as pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, and more, through <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Python tutorials<\/a>. You will learn to use flexible tools to clean, import, transform, combine, and restructure data.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Topics Covered<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Essential Python libraries like NumPy, pandas, and IPython<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Built-in data structures, functions, and files<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>How to <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/python\/applications\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">use Python<\/a> to manipulate, analyze, and clean data sets<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Data loading, storage, and file formats<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Plotting and visualization<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Data aggregation and group operations<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Practical examples showing how to apply Python in real-world<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Where to Buy &#8211; <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Python-Data-Analysis-Wes-Mckinney\/dp\/1491957662\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Python for Data Analysis: Data Wrangl<\/a><a href=\"https:\/\/www.amazon.in\/Python-Data-Analysis-Wes-Mckinney\/dp\/1491957662\">ing with pandas, NumPy, and Jupyter<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">10. Learning R: A Step-By-Step Function Guide to Data Analysis<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>&#8211; <\/strong><strong><em>Richard Cotton<\/em><\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"381\" height=\"500\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/learning-r-book.webp\" alt=\"DA Books for Beginner\" class=\"wp-image-12771\" 